@startuml
title Schatten - Direct Entra Login (local and production implemented; first production rollout F, v0.1.0)

actor Browser
participant "Application ingress\nCaddy / same-origin API" as Caddy
participant "FastAPI" as API
participant "Microsoft Entra ID\nDirect in both environments" as Provider
database PostgreSQL as DB

note over Provider
  One shared single-tenant confidential registration; separate dev/prod secrets.
  Exact tenant issuer; openid profile email; no Graph calls.
  No email_verified claim requirement; missing email prevents first linking.
  Registration permissions, consent, assignments and callbacks are shared.
end note

note over Browser, Caddy
  Development: https://app.localhost -> local Caddy -> HTTP API / Vite.
  Production: https://schatten.lupaus.eu -> Caddy TLS / React -> HTTP API.
  Entra Web callback is /api/v1/auth/callback at each exact origin.
  Post-logout return is /login at each origin; no Authentik or Traefik.
  Local Caddy/direct Entra and the production runtime are implemented; Coolify adapter removed.
end note

Browser -> Caddy : GET /api/v1/auth/login?return_to=/workspace
Caddy -> API : Fixed Host/proto and trusted client IP
API -> DB : Store hashed state + browser binding, nonce, PKCE
API --> Browser : 302 provider authorization URL\nHttpOnly pre-auth cookie
Browser -> Provider : Authorization Code + PKCE login
Provider --> Browser : Redirect with code + state
Browser -> Caddy : GET /api/v1/auth/callback?code=...&state=...
note right of Caddy
  Access log replaces code, state,
  error, error_description and
  session_state values with
  REDACTED.
end note
Caddy -> API : Callback with fixed proxy headers
API -> DB : Atomically consume browser-bound transaction
API -> Provider : Redeem code with confidential client + verifier
Provider --> API : Token response
API -> API : Validate signature, exact issuer, audience, nonce and claims
note right of DB
  Login never creates Users.
  Existing issuer/subject bindings are not rewritten.
  Each environment has an independent database.
end note
API -> DB : Guarded first-link to pre-provisioned User, or exact (issuer, subject)\nCreate hashed opaque application session
API --> Browser : 303 clean local path\nSecure HttpOnly SameSite=Strict cookie
Browser -> Caddy : GET SPA and /api with session cookie
Caddy -> API : Same-origin /api request
API -> DB : Reload active User and session
API --> Browser : Application data only; no provider token

@enduml
